            🌿 Wildlife Fact: Why Zanzibar Red Colobus Are Extraordinary
          </h4>
          <p style="color: #14532d; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
            Found nowhere else on planet Earth, the Zanzibar Red Colobus (*Piliocolobus kirkii*) has evolved uniquely on Unguja island. Unlike mainland monkeys, they have no opposable thumbs (an adaptation for fast brachiation through branches) and feed almost exclusively on unripe fruits and leaves because their complex multi-chambered stomachs cannot digest simple sugars. Because they are wild and habituated, visitors can observe family troops resting, grooming, and nursing from just meters away along the trail without feeding or intrusion.
          </p>
